  "body": {
    "id": "prop:rational-certificates",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For \\(P^\\star\\), the four SDC branch endpoint certificates are \\((x,y)=(0,29531/49500)\\), \\((0,200287/211500)\\), \\((1,54229/70500)\\), and \\((1,40731/49500)\\). Each vector has an interior coordinate, and cone multipliers \\((0,25/11)\\) certify the outer sharp endpoints; these multipliers lie outside the published normalized simplex.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "P_star",
      "r",
      "x_a",
      "lambda"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:strict-example",
      "def:branch-polytope",
      "def:interior-slack",
      "def:cone-duals",
      "thm:cone-endpoint-sharpness"
    ],
    "justification": "Exact rational certificates prevent the strict comparison from resting on floating-point optimization.",
    "gap": "No published example isolates a legal aggregate-support SDC law at which normalization loses both sharp outer endpoints.",
    "consumer": "The certificates form a reproducible regression test for any implementation of the sharp-set algorithm.",
    "proof_tex": "The exact covariance formulas (14) in \\(\\text{thm:cone-endpoint-sharpness}\\) give the following table by substitution:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c}\n(x,y)&\\theta_1&C_D&C_Z\\\\ \\hline\n(0,29531/49500)&711/1100&1019/13750&0\\\\\n(0,200287/211500)&3779/4700&0&2038/29375\\\\\n(1,54229/70500)&3779/4700&0&-312/29375\\\\\n(1,40731/49500)&911/1100&-78/6875&0\n\\end{array}                                                                    \\tag{20}\n\\]\nThe first two rows satisfy the positive branch and attain its lower and upper endpoints; the last two satisfy the negative branch and attain its lower and upper endpoints.  All four second coordinates lie in \\((0,1)\\), so (4) gives strictly positive slack for every certificate.\n\nFor the outer lower endpoint take \\(b=+1\\) and \\(\\lambda=(0,25/11)'\\).  The missing-cell instrument scores are \\(-14/25\\) and \\(11/25\\).  Hence the two box coefficients in the lower Lagrangian are\n\\[\n 1-\\lambda's_{(0,0)}=\\frac{25}{11}>0,\n \\qquad\n 1-\\lambda's_{(0,1)}=0.                                                        \\tag{21}\n\\]\nThe box minimization in the dual therefore selects \\(x=0\\), is indifferent to \\(y\\), and the first row of (20) supplies complementary slackness through \\(C_Z=0\\).  Equations (12) and (21) certify \\(711/1100\\).  For the outer upper endpoint take \\(b=-1\\) and the same multiplier.  The upper-dual coefficients are again those in (21), so box maximization selects \\(x=1\\), and the fourth row supplies \\(C_Z=0\\); this certifies \\(911/1100\\).  Finally\n\\[\n \\lambda_1+\\lambda_2=\\frac{25}{11}>1,\n\\]\nso both certificates are outside the normalized multiplier simplex.  This establishes every certificate without floating-point optimization.",
